{
  "info": {
    "name": "Laravel Roadmap \u2014 Task Manager API (Week 1-2)",
    "description": "Covers every endpoint built across Week 1 (service container, providers, facades, config, routing, middleware pipeline) and Week 2 (resource controllers, form requests, responses, real middleware, API resources) of the Laravel roadmap. Import this collection AND the paired environment file, select the environment in Postman's top-right dropdown, then use Collection Runner to run every request in order with its automated tests.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Task Manager \u2014 CRUD Lifecycle",
      "description": "Uses the three hardcoded seed tasks (ids 1/2/3) for most steps, since those are guaranteed to exist fresh on every single request. See the final two requests for an honest, deliberate demonstration of Week 2 Day 2's persistence caveat.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1. List Tasks (paginated)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/tasks",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "tasks"
              ]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 200', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Has a data array', function () { pm.expect(json.data).to.be.an('array'); });",
                  "pm.test('Has status_summary (Week 2 Day 5 ResourceCollection::with())', function () { pm.expect(json).to.have.property('status_summary'); });",
                  "pm.test('Has automatic pagination links/meta', function () { pm.expect(json).to.have.property('links'); pm.expect(json).to.have.property('meta'); });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "2. Get Seed Task #2 (IN_PROGRESS)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/tasks/2",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "tasks",
                "2"
              ]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 200', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Response is wrapped in a data key (JsonResource default)', function () { pm.expect(json).to.have.property('data'); });",
                  "pm.test('Task 2 seeds as IN_PROGRESS', function () { pm.expect(json.data.status).to.eql('IN_PROGRESS'); });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "2b. Attempt to Update WITHOUT Api Key (expect 401 \u2014 Week 2 Day 7 integration)",
          "description": "Day 4 built the 'secure-api' middleware group and only ever applied it to a standalone demo route. Day 7 finally applies it to the real Task API's write actions via TaskController::middleware() (Laravel 11's HasMiddleware). This request proves that protection is real: an update attempt with no X-Api-Key header is rejected before the business logic ever runs.",
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"title\": \"Should be rejected\",\n  \"status\": \"IN_PROGRESS\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/tasks/3",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "tasks",
                "3"
              ]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 401 \u2014 write is protected', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(401); });",
                  "// Note: index() and show() remain fully public \u2014 only",
                  "// store/update/destroy/markAsDone require the key."
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "3. Update Seed Task #3",
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Api-Key",
                "value": "{{api_key}}"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"title\": \"Updated via Postman\",\n  \"status\": \"IN_PROGRESS\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/tasks/3",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "tasks",
                "3"
              ]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 200', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Status was updated in THIS response', function () { pm.expect(json.data.status).to.eql('IN_PROGRESS'); });",
                  "// NOTE: this mutation is only visible in THIS request/response \u2014 a",
                  "// separate later GET /api/tasks/3 will show the ORIGINAL seed data",
                  "// again. See Week 2 Day 2's README for the full explanation."
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "4. Mark Seed Task #2 as Done (valid transition)",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Api-Key",
                "value": "{{api_key}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/tasks/2/done",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "tasks",
                "2",
                "done"
              ]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 200', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('success() macro envelope shape (Week 2 Day 3)', function () { pm.expect(json.success).to.eql(true); });",
                  "pm.test('Task is now DONE', function () { pm.expect(json.data.status).to.eql('DONE'); });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "5. Mark Seed Task #3 as Done Directly from TODO (expect 409)",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Api-Key",
                "value": "{{api_key}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/tasks/3/done",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "tasks",
                "3",
                "done"
              ]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Task 3 seeds as TODO \u2014 the business rule (Week 2 Day 3) rejects",
                  "// going straight to DONE without passing through IN_PROGRESS first.",
                  "pm.test('Status code is 409 Conflict', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(409); });",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('error() macro envelope shape', function () { pm.expect(json.success).to.eql(false); });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "6. Delete Seed Task #1",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Api-Key",
                "value": "{{api_key}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/tasks/1",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "tasks",
                "1"
              ]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 204 No Content', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(204); });",
                  "pm.test('Response body is empty', function () { pm.expect(pm.response.text()).to.eql(''); });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "7. Create a New Task (chained \u2014 see step 8)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Api-Key",
                "value": "{{api_key}}"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"title\": \"Created from Postman\",\n  \"status\": \"TODO\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/tasks",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "tasks"
              ]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 201 Created', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(201); });",
                  "pm.test('Has a Location header', function () { pm.response.to.have.header('Location'); });",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Created task has an id', function () { pm.expect(json.data.id).to.exist; });",
                  "// Captured for the NEXT request, which deliberately expects a 404 \u2014",
                  "// see that request's description for why.",
                  "pm.environment.set('created_task_id', json.data.id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "8. Verify Created Task Does NOT Persist (expected 404 \u2014 Week 2 Day 2 caveat)",
          "description": "This is NOT a broken test. Task::create() mutates an in-memory PHP static array \u2014 under the standard PHP execution model, the ENTIRE application boots fresh on every single HTTP request, so that array resets between step 7 and this step. A 404 here is the CORRECT, expected outcome, and is exactly what Week 2 Day 2's README explains in depth. Real persistence across requests arrives with Eloquent + a real database in Week 3.",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/tasks/{{created_task_id}}",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "tasks",
                "{{created_task_id}}"
              ]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 404 \u2014 proves the persistence caveat, not a bug', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(404);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
